# BouldersGate configuration
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. Never commit `.env`.

# NitroStack Configuration
NITRO_LOG_LEVEL=info
NITROSTACK_APP_MODE=universal

# Agent authentication
# =============================================================================
# Every BouldersGate tool is guarded by AgentApiKeyGuard. Keys are read from any
# environment variable starting with BOULDERSGATE_API_KEY. Define one variable per
# calling agent so each gets its own identity, quota, and audit trail.
#
# Note: the framework's own key loader reads only BOULDERSGATE_API_KEY_1,
# BOULDERSGATE_API_KEY_2, ... and a bare BOULDERSGATE_API_KEY. Named suffixes
# work because src/guards/agent-keys.ts collects them explicitly.
#
# Clients send the key in the tool call's `_meta.apiKey`, not an HTTP header —
# guards cannot see headers. See the README security section.
#
# The agent identity exposed to the protocol is a SHA-256 fingerprint of the
# key (`agent_<16 hex chars>`) — the key itself is never logged or returned.
#
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# These are placeholders. Replace them; do not ship these values.
# =============================================================================
BOULDERSGATE_API_KEY_DEMO=replace-with-a-random-64-char-hex-string
# BOULDERSGATE_API_KEY_CI=replace-with-a-different-random-string

# Demo mode (Optional, OFF by default)
# =============================================================================
# BOULDERSGATE_DEMO_NO_AUTH=true admits calls that present no valid key, under a
# single shared identity (`agent_demo`), so a public demo needs no credential.
#
# The cost: identity is what separates callers. With this on, every anonymous
# caller is the same agent, so any caller can execute in, list, and release any
# other caller's environments — on a public URL that runs code. Policy limits,
# offer TTLs, single-use offers, and the execution sandbox still apply.
#
# A valid key still authenticates normally and keeps its own identity. Only
# the literal string "true" enables this. Turn it off when the demo is over.
# =============================================================================
# BOULDERSGATE_DEMO_NO_AUTH=true

# Execution backend (Optional)
# =============================================================================
# BOULDERSGATE_BACKEND: docker | process | auto (default).
#   auto    - use Docker when a daemon answers, otherwise the process backend.
#   docker  - require a container backend; fail loudly when none is reachable.
#   process - always use the bounded-process backend.
# Leave unset on NitroCloud: Knative exposes no Docker daemon, so auto resolves
# to `process` there on its own.
# =============================================================================
# BOULDERSGATE_BACKEND=auto

# Server Transport Configuration (Optional)
# =============================================================================
# MCP_TRANSPORT_TYPE: Toggles transport mode. Values: stdio | http | dual.
# Defaults to 'stdio' in development and 'dual' in production/NODE_ENV=production.
# =============================================================================
# MCP_TRANSPORT_TYPE=stdio
# PORT=3000
# HOST=localhost
# ENABLE_CORS=true
